    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Lawrence Butler** (74.61) stands as our premier offensive weapon, benefiting from an elite matchup against Sugano (xERA 4.93). His high score is bolstered by a favorable platoon split and the prime lead-off spot, maximizing his chances to rack up R and SB. **Taylor Ward** (71.19) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (69.29) also grade out as strong starts; **Taylor Ward** benefits immensely from a hitter-friendly park and high wind speeds pushing fly balls, while **Geraldo Perdomo**\u2019s high score is driven largely by the favorable matchup against the vulnerable Abbott. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) remains a high-floor play in the UTIL spot, as his strong xwOBA profile and advantageous platoon split against Rodriguez provide significant depth to our daily output.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was bypassing **Bryson Stott** (37.77). While he remains a capable asset, his matchup against Harrison (xERA 3.39) coupled with a subpar platoon profile forced him below our 40.0 efficiency threshold. We are also managing significant roster attrition, as **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Yainer Diaz** all remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our ability to rotate out lower-scoring players like **Drew Gilbert** (40.12). We will monitor the lineup postings for **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman** against Rolison, as their shared matchup presents a moderate risk, though their placement at the top of the order keeps their efficiency scores viable for today\u2019s 5x5 objectives.",
